# Provide links or keys to any relevant tickets, articles or other resources
# Examples: Fixes #123, Closes #456, Ref: #789

# --- COMMIT END ---
# Type can be:
#    feat     (new feature)
#    fix      (bug fix)
#    docs     (changes to documentation)
#    test     (adding or changing tests)
#    refactor (refactoring production code)
#    perf     (performance improvements)
#    chore    (updating grunt tasks etc; no production code change)
#    ci       (changes to CI configuration)
#    build    (changes to build system)
# --------------------
# Scope examples for this project:
#    phase1, phase2, phase3, phase4, phase5
#    arduino, zkp, backend, frontend, docs, tests, deploy
# --------------------
# Remember to:
#   - Use imperative mood in subject line
#   - Do not end subject line with period
#   - Capitalize subject line and each paragraph
#   - Use body to explain what and why instead of how
#   - Separate subject from body with blank line
